{"name":"Blueberry Muffin","hex":"#5588ab","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blueberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edible round berry, belonging to the cowberry group (Vaccinium sect. Cyanococcus), with flared crowns at the end, that turns blue on ripening.","The shrub of the above-mentioned berry."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark blue colour.","Resembling or characteristic of blueberries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blueberry"},{"term":"muffin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of flattish bun, usually cut in two horizontally, toasted and spread with butter, etc., before being eaten.","A cupcake-shaped baked good (for example of cornbread, banana bread, or a chocolate dough), sometimes glazed but typically without frosting, eaten especially for breakfast (in contrast to a cupcake, which is a dessert)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To eat muffins.","To feed muffins to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muffin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Muffin","blocks":[{"text":"A muffin is a type of individual-sized baked good. It is often a small, sweet quickbread or cake in a cup-shaped container. It may be named for additional ingredients, e.g., the blueberry muffin contains blueberries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/NCI_Visuals_Food_Muffins.jpg/330px-NCI_Visuals_Food_Muffins.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muffin","wikidata":"Q207220"},{"title":"Blueberry","blocks":[{"text":"Blueberries are a widely distributed and widespread group of perennial flowering plants with blue or purple berries. They are classified in the section Cyanococcus within the genus Vaccinium. Commercial blueberries—both wild (lowbush) and cultivated (highbush)—are all native to North America. The highbush varieties were introduced into Europe during the 1930s."}],"image":"h